===Etymology===
[[File:Saga Oseberg Details Rope coil curl spiral on timber deck near stern aft Taukveil på skipsdekk Viking ship replica 2012 Tønsberg harbour havn Norway 2019-08-16 04324.jpg|thumb|A flemish ''(noun sense)'' or [[Flemish coil]] of [[rope#Noun|rope]] on the [[deck#Noun|deck]] of the ''[[:no:Saga Oseberg|Saga Oseberg]]'', a [[Norwegian#Adjective|Norwegian]] [[replica]] of a [[Viking#Adjective|Viking]] [[ship#Noun|ship]].]]

The {{glossary|noun}} is an {{ellipsis|en|Flemish coil|nocap=1}}, so called because the technique of coiling rope in this manner began with sailors from Flanders.

The {{glossary|verb}} is from {{m|en|Flemish|t=of or relating to Flanders|pos=adjective}},<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=''v.''{{sup|1}}|noformat=1|id=71453|date=September 2018}}</ref> from ''Flemish coil''.

